   "caption": "This clause is exclusivity in disguise. Read it before you sign.\n\n\"Brand gets first refusal on future deals\" sounds polite. Exclusivity covers the deal itself. First refusal kicks in when it ends: the brand can match a new offer and keep you, and you can't sign anyone else until they answer.\n\nMake it fair:\n1. A short answer window (one creator-contract guide calls 5-14 days typical)\n2. Define \"match\": same fee, deliverables and dates\n3. If they pass or stay silent, you're free\n4. The right ends on a set date\n5. Or price it as a paid add-on, like exclusivity\n\nRed flag: no release when they say no. That's open-ended exclusivity.\n\nNot legal advice. Get big contracts checked.\n\nSend this to a creator who's about to sign.\n\n#branddeals #creatorbusiness #influencertips #contentcreator #ugccreator #freelancetips",
   "keyword": null,
   "pillar": 4,
   "topic": "Right of first refusal vs exclusivity in brand deals: answer window, define match, release on no, end date or fee",
   "sources": [
    "https://www.makeinfluence.com/en/academy/right-of-first-refusal-and-renewal-options-in-influencer-contracts",
    "https://www.creatoressentials.com/glossary/right-of-first-refusal/"
   ]
