   "caption": "Your reel isn't boring. It has dead air. Save this for your next edit.\n\nThe dead-air pass (do it before any effects):\n1. Breaths: start every sentence on the first word\n2. Fillers: so, um, basically, like. If the line works without it, cut it\n3. Endings: the pause after each point and the trailing \"yeah\"\n\nCuts look jumpy? Punch in a little on every other cut.\n\nExample: a 48-second take with 17 seconds of silence ends up at 31. Your numbers will differ, but the pass is the same.\n\nRule of thumb: if nothing changes for 3 seconds, cut or add text.\n\nSend this to the friend whose reels start with a breath.\n\n#reelstips #videoediting #contentcreator #editingtips #instagramreels #creatortips",
   "keyword": null,
   "pillar": 2,
   "topic": "Dead-air pass: cut breaths, fillers and endings before effects; punch in to hide jump cuts",
   "sources": [
    "https://manychat.com/blog/instagram-trends-for-creators-2026/"
   ]
